From 6665b363b812f90097325b7693a9b55ab83adf57 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 21:05:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Pivot to v2: the kid self-introduction e-name card
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

MINIMEE v2 is the child equivalent of an adult's commercial e-name card:
one shareable link that says who the child is, what they like, shows their
self-introduction video and MEE card collection, and carries the lost-item
channel. v1's two-video-per-theme production pipeline is deliberately not
part of this surface — a card has at most one video, so there is a single
thing to generate, retry and show.

- src/lib/kidCard.ts: the card model plus two worked examples. Parents
  landing on the site see what the product IS rather than a feature list,
  and the examples are labelled so nobody mistakes them for a real child.
- KidCardPage: the public card at /kid/:slug. No account needed, because a
  grandparent, a teacher, or whoever found a lost water bottle has to be
  able to open it. The lost-item section only renders when the parent has
  switched lost mode on, and routes through /lost/:token so no contact
  details are ever exposed.
- PixelWorldGame + /play: a long left-to-right pixel world where walking
  into a pickup collects it. Movement and collection only — no pet stats,
  no jump physics — it has to be fun on a phone in thirty seconds.
  Keyboard and touch both drive it.
- Home page now leads with the e-name card story and links straight to a
  live example and the playable demo.

Build passes and all 29 tests pass.
